        schema:contentUrl  <https://silknow.org/silknow/media/vam/O364979_5.jpg> , <http://media.vam.ac.uk/media/thira/collection_images/2014GX/2014GX1192.jpg> .

<http://data.silknow.org/event/31fc1545-2820-3434-9741-74f143c546a3>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "From a set of five hangings (T.161 to 165-1931). \nThe set of five tapestries formerly hung in the drawing room of the donor's home at 25 Grosvenor Square, London. She bought them at an anonymous sale in Paris (Vente X) on 17 December, 1900. She paid 55,000 francs for the set.\n\nIn her catalogue of tapestries in the Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York, under catalogue number 34 (a version of <i>Autumn</i> from a related series), Edith Standen notes that the V&amp;A's series of <i>Seasons</i> may be the one referred to as \"formerly in the Baumgarten collection, [New York], with borders missing\" in George Leland Hunter's <i>The Practical Book of Tapestries</i>, (1925), p.156.\n\nStanden also notes a number of variations on the subject, likely to have been designed by van Schoor, in other collections."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/c1f9f32a-cadb-3014-9599-50adf81f3408> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Presented in memory of Mrs Letitia Willet Garrison, by her sister, Miss Lillie Bell Randell" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/555a17c2-86ba-3f37-9bc7-ff359e1e064f> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "From a set of five hangings (T.161 to 165-1931). \nThe set of five tapestries formerly hung in the drawing room of the donor's home at 25 Grosvenor Square, London. She bought them at an anonymous sale in Paris (Vente X) on 17 December, 1900. She paid 55,000 francs for the set.\n\nIn her catalogue of tapestries in the Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York, under catalogue number 34 (a version of <i>Autumn</i> from a related series), Edith Standen notes that the V&amp;A's series of <i>Seasons</i> may be the one referred to as \"formerly in the Baumgarten collection, [New York], with borders missing\" in George Leland Hunter's <i>The Practical Book of Tapestries</i>, (1925), p.156.\n\nStanden also notes a number of variations on the subject, likely to have been designed by van Schoor, in other collections."@en .

