<http://data.silknow.org/object/555a17c2-86ba-3f37-9bc7-ff359e1e064f/observation/4>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/historical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Standen (citing Wauters, <i>Tapisseries bruxelloises</i>, pp.355-6, 358) notes that a set of <i>De Vier Tyden van het Jaer</i>, after van Schoor, was bought from the weaver van den Hecke by King William III of England between 1690 and 1700 for his friend, Everard van Weede van Dijkveld."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/555a17c2-86ba-3f37-9bc7-ff359e1e064f> .

